        <div class="faq-list">
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>I've broken down on the Anderson Drive section of the A90 in Aberdeen — is that different to the open road?<span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg></span></summary>
            <p>Anderson Drive carries A90 traffic through the city itself, so it mixes dual-carriageway speeds with signalised junctions and roundabouts such as Haudagain and the Anderson Drive/Great Western Road junction. There's often less run-off space than on the open trunk road, so getting fully clear of the traffic lane matters just as much, if not more. Tell us which junction or landmark you're closest to when you call.</p>
          </details>
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>Is it safe to wait in my car if I've broken down on the A90?<span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg></span></summary>
            <p>It depends on where you've stopped. If you're on a verge, in a layby, or otherwise well clear of the running lanes, staying in the vehicle with your seatbelt on is usually the safer option while you wait, especially in poor weather. If you're still partly in a live lane and can't move further off safely, get yourself and any passengers out and behind a barrier or well away from the carriageway, then call for help.</p>
          </details>
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>Do you cover the A90 all the way to Peterhead and Stonehaven, or just the Aberdeen stretch?<span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg></span></summary>
            <p>We recover breakdowns on the A90 both north and south of Aberdeen, including the Portlethen and Stonehaven direction and the Bridge of Don, Ellon and Peterhead direction, as well as through the city itself. Give us your location when you call and we'll confirm we can reach you.</p>
          </details>
        </div>
      </div>
